MinidumpMiscInfoDebugBuildString() enumerates OS_MAC/OS_IOS/OS_ANDROID/
OS_LINUX/OS_CHROMEOS/OS_WIN/OS_FUCHSIA and #errors on anything else:

    ../../third_party/crashpad/crashpad/minidump/minidump_misc_info_writer.cc:123:2:
    error: #error define kOS for this operating system

Crashpad's own tree already has real OS_HAIKU handling in numerous
neighboring files (util/misc/address_types.h, util/misc/capture_context.h,
util/posix/signals.cc, util/posix/symbolic_constants_posix.cc,
util/process/process_id.h -- the last one patched here already in 0057);
this one function was simply never given a Haiku branch. Confirmed this gap
exists in the pinned upstream revision itself (not something our tree
diverged into), so it is a genuine upstream omission, not a QtWebEngine
source-drop artifact.

kOS here only feeds a human-readable debug build string embedded in the
minidump ("dbghelp.i386,...,<kOS>"), so "haiku" is the honest value -- it
does not need to match any enum or generated constant the way the field
trial platform name did (0056).

--- a/chromium/third_party/crashpad/crashpad/minidump/minidump_misc_info_writer.cc
+++ b/chromium/third_party/crashpad/crashpad/minidump/minidump_misc_info_writer.cc
@@ -117,6 +117,8 @@
   static constexpr char kOS[] = "win";
 #elif defined(OS_FUCHSIA)
   static constexpr char kOS[] = "fuchsia";
+#elif defined(OS_HAIKU)
+  static constexpr char kOS[] = "haiku";
 #else
 #error define kOS for this operating system
 #endif
